widgets_values:
{"version": 1, "tone": "icon", "look": "card", "step": 1, "icon": "microchip", "text": "**Model Info** reads which model is loaded. A derivation in the **Render** Context turns `$model_family` into `$size` (like `832x1216`), `$sampler` and `$cfg`, and each **Var →** node reads one into a widget: **Width** takes the first number of `$size`, **Height** the second.

:pi-sync: Switch it off in WP Toggles, or bypass **Model Info** (Ctrl+B): the **Mode Relay** passes that on to the **Node Group**, and the latent and sampler use their own widgets again.

[Model Info](docs:wp-model-info){button pi-microchip} [Mode Relay](docs:wp-mode-relay){button pi-share-alt} [Node Group](docs:wp-node-group){button pi-objects-column}", "color": "warning", "bookmark": {"anchor": "custom", "view": {"x": 3750, "y": 1810}, "zoomMode": "fixed", "zoom": 0.6, "shortcut": "Alt+5", "order": 5}}

